# Ten Minutes | INT | Lecture Theatre, Bench | DAY | blok, hartwell | Cover it | A limerick is coming through. He muffles the inker with his coat and cues the professor to talk louder. The real message arrives on the minute. Applause | Nobody notices | 6 | crowd=400, props=paper tape
# The Hunt | INT | Newspaper Office | DAY | blok, the_manager | Read the answer | The professor's letter: scientific hooliganism. Four days on, a reply, signed. A magician. The manager wants a writ | The culprit names himself | 4 | props=newspapers
# The Hunt | EXT | Music Hall Roof | DAY | blok, marchmont | Confront him | A ten-foot mast among chimney pots. A spark coil in a hatbox. If I can do this, he says pleasantly, what could a navy do? | | 6 | props=aerial mast+spark coil
# The Hunt | INT | Magician's Workshop | NIGHT | blok, marchmont | See how it is done | Trick cabinets, a mind-reading act run by wireless for years. {blok} shows him, despite himself, where the tuning leaks worst | {blok} admits the flaw | 5 | props=stage illusions
# The Rematch | INT | Lecture Theatre | NIGHT | blok, marchmont, hartwell, the_manager | Let it through | A staged test before the press. {blok} is told to detune against interference. He does not. The inker prints a courteous greeting from the roof next door. He reads it out | The flaw is shown in public | 7 | crowd=400, props=wireless receiver
# The Rematch | INT | Music Hall, Stage Door | DAY | blok, marchmont | Start work | Sacked at six. At ten next morning, a stage door, worse pay, a handshake, and a cabinet that needs rewiring | | 3 | props=toolbag
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; drawn from the interruption of a wireless demonstration in London in 1903, with invented people
